<!-- ═════════ 09. METHODOLOGY ═════════ -->
<div class="container"><details class="accordion"><summary class="accordion-header"><div class="accordion-num">09</div><div class="accordion-text"><span class="accordion-title">Methodology</span><span class="accordion-subtitle">Sample design, statistics, coding, known gaps</span></div><div class="accordion-icon">+</div></summary><div class="accordion-body">

<h3>9a. Sample design</h3>
<div class="stat-grid"><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-num">300</div><div class="stat-label">Participants</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-num">15</div><div class="stat-label">Questions per participant</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-num">417K</div><div class="stat-label">Words analyzed</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-num">83</div><div class="stat-label">Thematic codes</div></div></div>
<p>All 300 participants were Canadian adults age 30 to 60 living in British Columbia or Alberta who had switched their primary personal checking bank within the past 24 months. Quota-balanced to oversample the four highest-priority banks (CIBC, Simplii, RBC, TD at n=60 each) relative to BMO and Scotiabank (n=30 each). The 15-question interview covered brand mental availability (split-sample CEP battery: CEPs 1, 4, 5 to Set A n=150; CEPs 2, 3, 6 to Set B n=150), previous-bank push forces, evaluation and selection, current experience, wallet composition, forward-looking propensity, and macro sentiment. Fresh-prompt design prevents cross-CEP conditioning; split-sample integrity verified.</p>

<h3>9b. Statistical methodology</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Alpha:</strong> 0.10 two-tailed (convention at this sample size and subgroup structure).</li>
<li><strong>Default test:</strong> two-proportion z-test when every expected cell count is &ge;5. <strong>Fallback:</strong> Fisher's exact test when any expected cell is &lt;5.</li>
<li><strong>Benchmark convention:</strong> dashed line on bar charts displays the overall sample average; the test compares the focal subgroup against all OTHER respondents combined.</li>
<li><strong>Three-tier rule:</strong><em>Strong</em> = significant, recommendation language permitted; <em>Hedge</em> = non-significant but corroborated by an independent signal, "directionally" language only; <em>No-claim</em> = non-significant and uncorroborated, not highlighted. Finding 6 is the single hedge in this report.</li>
</ul>

<h3>9c. Coding and reliability</h3>
<div class="stat-grid"><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-num">83</div><div class="stat-label">Thematic codes</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-num">0.929</div><div class="stat-label">Thematic Kappa<br>(Almost Perfect)</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-num">0.970</div><div class="stat-label">Direction Kappa</div></div><div class="stat-card"><div class="stat-num">0.472</div><div class="stat-label">Intensity Kappa</div></div></div>
<p>Dual independent Sonnet 4 coders with Opus 4 arbiter on disagreements. Each meaning unit received a thematic code plus a direction tag (positive/negative/neutral). Each (participant, code) pair also received a 1&ndash;3 intensity score. Intensity Kappa fell below the threshold for headline use due to marginal skew (most scores at level 2 or 3); intensity is reported as a coloring layer on top of the binary mention rate.</p>

<h3>9d. Known gaps</h3>
<div class="caveat"><ul>
<li><strong>Sample is recent switchers age 30 to 60 in BC and Alberta only.</strong> Findings characterize this cohort, not Simplii's full customer base.</li>
<li><strong>Fee-creep-over-time frustration code at zero everywhere.</strong> Genuine, not a coding bug. Participants switched within 24 months and have not been at the new bank long enough to experience fee creep.</li>
</ul></div>

</div></details></div>

<!-- Verbatim drill-down modal -->
<div class="vb-overlay" id="vbOverlay" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="vb-dialog" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="vbTitle">
    <button type="button" class="vb-close" id="vbClose" aria-label="Close">&times;</button>
    <div class="vb-header">
      <h3 id="vbTitle"></h3>
      <p class="vb-q" id="vbSubtitle"></p>
    </div>
    <div class="vb-body" id="vbBody"></div>
  </div>
</div>

<script is:inline>
(function () {
  var VX = window.__VX;
  if (!VX) return;

  var overlay = document.getElementById('vbOverlay');
  var titleEl = document.getElementById('vbTitle');
  var subEl = document.getElementById('vbSubtitle');
  var bodyEl = document.getElementById('vbBody');
  var closeBtn = document.getElementById('vbClose');
  if (!overlay || !titleEl || !subEl || !bodyEl || !closeBtn) return;

  function escHtml(s) {
    var d = document.createElement('div');
    d.appendChild(document.createTextNode(s == null ? '' : String(s)));
    return d.innerHTML;
  }

  function intensityLabel(i) {
    if (i === 3) return 'Narrative';
    if (i === 2) return 'Elaborated';
    return 'Brief';
  }

  function renderCard(ex) {
    var isSimplii = ex.bank === 'Simplii';
    var cardClass = 'vb-card ' + (isSimplii ? 'bank-Simplii' : 'bank-other');
    var intClass = 'vb-intensity i' + (ex.intensity || 2);
    var tags = [];
    if (ex.bank) tags.push({label: ex.bank, cls: 'bank'});
    if (ex.age) tags.push({label: ex.age, cls: ''});
    if (ex.prov) tags.push({label: ex.prov, cls: ''});
    if (ex.area) tags.push({label: ex.area, cls: ''});
    tags.push({label: 'Q' + (ex.qid || '').replace(/^Q/, ''), cls: ''});

    var html = '<div class="' + cardClass + '">';
    html += '<div class="vb-quote">&ldquo;' + escHtml(ex.quote) + '&rdquo;</div>';
    html += '<div class="vb-tags">';
    html += '<span class="' + intClass + '">' + intensityLabel(ex.intensity) + '</span>';
    tags.forEach(function (t) {
      html += '<span class="vb-tag ' + t.cls + '">' + escHtml(t.label) + '</span>';
    });
    html += '</div></div>';
    return html;
  }

  function openModal(chartId, barLabel) {
    var chart = VX.charts[chartId];
    if (!chart) return;
    var codeNames = chart.bars[barLabel];
    if (!codeNames) return;
    var qids = chart.qids || [];
    var codeSet = {};
    codeNames.forEach(function (cn) { codeSet[cn] = true; });

    // Find every (participant, qid) pair where the participant's codes at that
    // qid include any of the bar's code names. Emit one card per pair so a
    // participant who cited the theme in both Q5 and Q8 gets both quotes shown.
    var cards = [];
    (VX.participants || []).forEach(function (p) {
      qids.forEach(function (qid) {
        var pcodes = (p.c || {})[qid];
        if (!pcodes || !pcodes.length) return;
        // Find which of the bar's codes this participant has at this qid
        var matched = null;
        for (var i = 0; i < pcodes.length; i++) {
          if (codeSet[pcodes[i]]) { matched = pcodes[i]; break; }
        }
        if (!matched) return;
        var verbatim = (p.v || {})[qid];
        if (!verbatim) return;
        var intensity = ((p.i || {})[qid] || {})[matched] || 2;
        cards.push({
          pid: p.pid,
          qid: qid,
          quote: verbatim,
          direction: '~',
          intensity: intensity,
          bank: p.bank,
          age: p.age,
          prov: p.prov,
          area: p.area,
          code: matched,
        });
      });
    });

    // Sort: Simplii first (all are Simplii here, kept for future generality),
    // then by intensity desc (most narrative-weighted quotes first),
    // then by participant id for stable order.
    cards.sort(function (a, b) {
      var sa = a.bank === 'Simplii' ? 0 : 1;
      var sb = b.bank === 'Simplii' ? 0 : 1;
      if (sa !== sb) return sa - sb;
      var ia = a.intensity || 0;
      var ib = b.intensity || 0;
      if (ia !== ib) return ib - ia;
      return a.pid - b.pid;
    });

    // Count unique participants (cards may contain multiple quotes per participant
    // when a chart spans multiple qids and the participant mentioned the theme at
    // more than one qid).
    var uniquePids = {};
    cards.forEach(function (c) { uniquePids[c.pid] = true; });
    var nQuoted = Object.keys(uniquePids).length;

    // Parse "Simplii switchers (n=60)" into label + total. Falls back gracefully
    // if the cohort string doesn't match the expected pattern.
    var cohortLabel = chart.cohort || '';
    var cohortTotal = null;
    var m = /^(.*?)\s*\(n=(\d+)\)\s*$/.exec(cohortLabel);
    if (m) {
      cohortLabel = m[1];
      cohortTotal = parseInt(m[2], 10);
    }

    if (cards.length === 0) {
      titleEl.textContent = barLabel + '  ·  ' + (chart.cohort || '');
      subEl.textContent = chart.question || '';
      bodyEl.innerHTML = '<p class="vb-empty">No participant quotes matched this theme at that question.</p>';
    } else {
      var titleSuffix = nQuoted + (cohortTotal ? ' of ' + cohortTotal : '') +
        (cohortLabel ? ' ' + cohortLabel : '') + ' quoted';
      titleEl.textContent = barLabel + '  ·  ' + titleSuffix;
      subEl.textContent = chart.question || '';
      var quoteWord = cards.length === 1 ? 'quote' : 'quotes';
      var introText = 'Showing ' + cards.length + ' ' + quoteWord +
        ' from ' + nQuoted + ' participant' + (nQuoted === 1 ? '' : 's') +
        ' coded to this theme. Intensity tag shows narrative depth.';
      var intro = '<p class="vb-empty" style="margin:0 0 12px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);">' +
        escHtml(introText) + '</p>';
      bodyEl.innerHTML = intro + cards.map(renderCard).join('');
    }

    overlay.classList.add('open');
    overlay.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'false');
    document.body.style.overflow = 'hidden';
  }

  function closeModal() {
    overlay.classList.remove('open');
    overlay.setAttribute('aria-hidden', 'true');
    document.body.style.overflow = '';
  }

  closeBtn.addEventListener('click', closeModal);
  overlay.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
    if (e.target === overlay) closeModal();
  });
  document.addEventListener('keydown', function (e) {
    if (e.key === 'Escape' && overlay.classList.contains('open')) closeModal();
  });

  // Click delegation: any row inside a data-drilldown-chart container opens the modal
  document.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
    var row = e.target.closest('[data-drilldown-chart] .bar-row, [data-drilldown-chart] .stack-bar-row');
    if (!row) return;
    var chartEl = row.closest('[data-drilldown-chart]');
    if (!chartEl) return;
    var chartId = chartEl.getAttribute('data-drilldown-chart');
    var labelEl = row.querySelector('.bar-label, .stack-bar-label');
    if (!labelEl) return;
    // Strip any trailing sig superscript or markup, use only the text content
    var label = (labelEl.textContent || '').replace(/\*+\s*$/, '').trim();
    openModal(chartId, label);
  });
})();
</script>

</body>
</html>
